  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\r\n\r\nThis conditional interface certificate completes the reverse centre phase complementary to PR1708. For two disjoint 112-row panels sharing the same eight **post-A sinks** and corresponding exact native operators/charts, gathering both panels before each return preserves the signed persistent endpoint and returns the same eight arbitrary-input scratch rows to zero. It reduces the literal reverse-phase bill from 416 to 384 macros: 16\u21928 rank-8 children, 368\u2192360 ADDs, and 32\u219216 CLEARs. All 352 panel reads remain charged.\r\n\r\nThe positive gather envelope doubles from 11/2 to 11. The written exact linear-prefix argument includes unchanged child-private dirt; one extra magnitude bit covers this local envelope comparison. Every fused primitive is therefore conservatively priced at mu+1, with additional preparation/routing/restoration/ownership/hosting overhead DeltaH. A saving requires 8 R8(mu+1)+360 ADD(mu+1)+16 CLEAR(mu+1)+DeltaH < 16 R8(mu)+368 ADD(mu)+32 CLEAR(mu). No native tariff, eligible selected-call pair, full-call recurrence or new kappa is admitted. CLEAR makes the full scratch map singular; the adjoint statement concerns the persistent block.\r\n\r\n## Task and overlap\r\n\r\nBase: 0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea. Revision-3 card: centre-path-sharing; nonce 1e94dbbfba8c1dc58dbab4dcba380ae3; scope key 184695337cedab03152e/selected-eight-centers/backward-two-panel-shared-return/weighted-guard. Scope is refined because [PR1708](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1708), head 4d163c04c0980c5b0e9092fbd5864c7cfadc125d, already covers the forward fanout. This adds the selected backward event binding and precision-sensitive invoice, without claiming new generic batching algebra. [PR751](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/751) and [PR830](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/830) are credited predecessors; their exact heads are in TASK.json.\r\n\r\n[Claim and handoff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1516#discussioncomment-18919192). Final overlap search covered 419 open PR bodies including drafts and 873 local records; relevant Discussions were read directly. Numbered pages are non-atomic, and no complete Discussion census or novelty certificate is claimed. Current main and PR1708's head were rechecked before submission.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nRun:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/centre-shared-return-guard\r\n```\r\n\r\nPython 3.12.14, macOS arm64: registered replay passes, all 480 complex basis inputs match an independent closed-form endpoint, and seven semantic fault witnesses fail as required. Eight phase-bearing two-coordinate Gaussian unitary representatives exercise the abstract inverse-adjoint interface; this is not an actual 512-dimensional operator replay. Exact coefficients and all eight reverse blocks are pinned to selected-replay.tar.gz. Written linearity handles arbitrary exact common operators under the stated hypotheses.\r\n\r\nAll 18 repository onboarding tests pass. Standalone exports pass normally and under -O; input/receipt corruption and occupied-output controls reject safely. VALIDATION.json records evidence and limitations. No full frontier replay, Lean, native rounded precision theorem or hosting admission was run. Selected record and frozen sources are unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Credit\r\n\r\nCredit Cinna Davis/1337isnot1337 (PR1708), Sagar Thakrar (PR751), Ryan Haines (PR830), Scratch-net (private-centre adjoint/CLEAR audit), Jeremy Kothe and the retained construction/auditor/compiler lineage listed in README and TASK. Generic adjoint/batching algebra is prior work. Prepared by @ToikY with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in mathematics, implementation, bounded independent review, tests and writing. Apache-2.0; original notices retained. No independent human review.\r\n\r\n## Open next questions\r\n\r\n[README next questions](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/blob/ea14f191752c9901bf6684763534d2d248fb2ad2/research/centre-shared-return-guard/README.md#open-next-questions): trace one actual caller pair to prove common post-A sinks, charts and uninterrupted ownership, then instantiate the native precision/tape prices and DeltaH. Those are blockers to a complete-call or frontier improvement. No merge or frontier update is requested.\r\n",
